# Build output
/bin/
/_output/
/dist/

# Go
*.test
*.out


# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Coverage profiles
cover*.out

# Project-local pinned tool binaries (task tools)
/.tools/

# BuildKit cache + build output (task build:qemu)
/.cache/
/_output/
# ...and _output as a symlink. The trailing-slash form above matches directories
# only, so a worktree that symlinks _output at the primary checkout's build
# output shows it as an untracked *file* and the next `git add -A` commits the
# link — with an absolute path that means nothing on any other machine.
/_output

# Coverage intermediates
cover.raw

# pgregory.net/rapid writes a reproducer here when a property test fails. It is a
# scratch artefact of one run on one machine: rapid replays it on the next run, so a
# committed one makes every developer re-run a case that was fixed — and two of them
# were committed by accident (2026-08-01, 2026-08-02) before this line existed. A case
# worth keeping permanently belongs in the test as a named example.
testdata/rapid/

# go-task's checksum cache. Committing it makes any `task build:guest` dirty the
# tree, and the value is a function of the machine that produced it, not of the
# sources — it was committed once by accident and was already stale by the next run.
/.task/

# The agent harness's local settings and scratch workflows.
/.claude/
